 "description": "Koo2013 - Shear stress induced calcium influx and eNOS activation - Model 1\nBioModels BIOMD0000000464 (curated). SBML file: BIOMD0000000464_url.xml.\nSimulation: 0 to 100000 time units (SED-ML: BIOMD0000000464_url.sedml (auto-generated placeholder); duration chosen from the dynamics: still changing at cap), sampling 100.\nRun switches: -ig:mass -INT:1 -obeymaxint\nVerification against libRoadRunner (SBML reference): PASS, max |difference| = 2.04e-06 of species peak (worst: s10)\nSBML time units are used unchanged as Kintecus seconds.\nConversion notes:\n  [info] 's7' goes below zero in the SBML: integrated as s7_o = value + 10000000, output as s7 = OUTC[s7_o;-10000000*source]\n  [info] 's11' goes below zero in the SBML: integrated as s11_o = value + 1000000000, output as s11 = OUTC[s11_o;-1000000000*source]\n  [info] 's13' goes below zero in the SBML: integrated as s13_o = value + 200000, output as s13 = OUTC[s13_o;-200000*source]\n  [info] re5: rate not proportional to its reactants; written once as signed lines (source+S[USER;...]) for s7_o\n  [info] re7 term 2/3: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] re8: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] re9: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] re12: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed",
